  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Please consider adding keyboard bindings to allow for switching the stream camera between pins. This would enable streamers/performers to use external input devices to switch the active camera position instead of having to pick up and interact with the camera on screen/inside of VR. \n\nFor example, a solo performer could use a foot pedal or other HID input to seamlessly swap the camera without having to take their hands away from playing an instrument, operating DJ decks, etc.\n\nAlternatively, this could be exposed as an OSC input accepting an integer input to indicate a pinned camera view should be active. This would avoid the need to introduce additional keybinds if additional pins are subsequently added to the camera. [1]\n\nIf implemented via OSC this could be accomplished as part of the larger \"Expose VRC Camera to OSC\" feature request. [2]\n\n[1] https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/add-more-pins-and-a-dolly-system-for-vrchat-cameras\n\n[2] https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/expose-vrc-camera-to-osc",
